{"availability":"available","full":"Alhadis/Atom-GitHubSyntax","name":"Atom-GitHubSyntax","description":"Up-to-date syntax theme for Atom that matches GitHub's motif, including day/night mode.","category":"Other","language":"Less","stars":4,"forks":0,"created":"2022-02-26T07:12:55Z","updated":"2023-04-02T22:52:32Z","license":"ISC","branch":"master","homepage":"https://atom.io/themes/atom-github-syntax","topics":["atom","atom-theme","syntax-highlighting","syntax-theme"],"demo":"https://git.io/Jf1IY","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T00:29:41.569Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T00:29:41.569Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T00:29:41.569Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T00:29:41.569Z","stars":4,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This is a syntax highlighting theme for Atom that replicates the exact appearance of highlighted source-code on GitHub.com. It was created to facilitate development of TextMate-compatible grammars for use on GitHub.","GitHub uses TextMate selectors to map tokenised scope-lists onto CSS classes. In rare cases, a grammar might specify a scope-list that TextMate and CSS selectors interpret differently. For example, consider the following pattern:","GitHub recognises both the variable and variable.other scopes, and assigns a different colour to each. On GitHub, the aforementioned rule will be highlighted as the former (variable), whereas a naïve theme targeting .variable.other in CSS will see the latter."],"features":["Automatic dark-mode detected from system settings. Support for high-contrast and “dimmed” theme variants. Support for colourblind users (protanopia, deuteranopia, tritanopia) Pathologically-accurate highlighting (see…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Alhadis/Atom-GitHubSyntax/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"9edbf2e689fc49da93ca1147591eb73d840e6118594aaaf0950696ecfb0c0fe5","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T00:29:41.651Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T00:29:41.65